Let's also maybe include the 8x8 pair diagram: For each 2x4 rectangle:
\begin{array}{cccc}
A&B&C&D\\
C&D&A&B
\end{array}
But note if bottom row C D A B, then A positions (top1,bottom3): row diff 1 col diff 2; B top2 bottom4; C top3 bottom1; D top4 bottom2. Yes. Tiling 8x8: four horizontal strips of height 2; each strip split into two 2x4 blocks. Thus 8 blocks × 4 pairs = 32 pairs. At most one per pair -> ≤32.
